WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.940
Welcome to the Federal Modernization
Workbook's developer workbook,

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.287
Building the Attribute-Driven Migration.

3
00:00:06.287 --> 00:00:11.462
This is Chapter 9: drift pipelines
and evidence to the ISSO.

4
00:00:11.462 --> 00:00:15.063
A check that runs when someone
remembers is a spot check.

5
00:00:15.063 --> 00:00:18.676
A check that runs every day,
says what moved since yesterday,

6
00:00:18.676 --> 00:00:23.175
and leaves evidence nobody can edit
afterward is continuous monitoring.

7
00:00:23.175 --> 00:00:28.298
We'll start from Learn's sample workflows
for signing in from GitHub Actions without

8
00:00:28.298 --> 00:00:31.739
a secret, see what they leave
out, then walk the comparison,

9
00:00:31.739 --> 00:00:35.325
the findings, the evidence
package, two labs and the dangers.

10
00:00:35.325 --> 00:00:40.540
One note before we begin: the code is
illustrative, tested against fixtures.
